Reason: port: a stage change (TMarDirector::setNextStage) to an episode past the end of its area's list in the stage table loads no scene: mountStageArchive returns nothing, TMarDirector::loadResource returns before it creates the guide's archive, and TGuide::load faults setting the font of a pane its empty screen does not have (SIGSEGV at 0x150, J2DTextBox::setFont). Retail never asks for such an episode. Super Mario Eclipse does when Mario leaves Lighthouse Island's interior (area 79, episode 1) at the top of the lighthouse: it returns to Lighthouse Island (area 62) in the episode of mPrevArea, which after the warp menu or a position-only save state load is the stage the warp left (Delfino Plaza's episode 8, say), and Lighthouse Island has episodes 0 to 7 (sms-launcher#312). Take the episode the player chose for the world (0x40003, which the episode select and the warps record) instead, or the first.
